<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ipswich, Massachusetts</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ipswich is a town on the North Shore of Massachusetts, founded by English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puritans">Puritans</a> in 1634. In 1687 its townspeople, led by the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-wise">John Wise</a>, refused to pay taxes imposed by Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edmund-andros">Edmund Andros</a> without an elected assembly, and their leaders were tried and punished. The episode is remembered as an early protest against taxation without representation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ipswich-massachusetts.jpg" alt="Ipswich, Massachusetts" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Quintin Soloviev · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ipswich,_Massachusetts.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
